  "body": "## What changed\n- Added viewport picking for 2D Contour **Start point** and **Exit point** on the **Lead in / Lead out** tab (`crates/ui/src/start_exit_pick.rs`, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/start_exit_rows.rs`, `crates/ui/src/egui_app/op_page.rs`).\n- Added **Pick start** / **Pick exit** buttons (switching to **Stop picking** when armed) in each group header and **Clear start** / **Clear exit** buttons inside the enabled groups.\n- Unlocked off-Geometry-tab picking (`crates/ui/src/interact.rs`) and routed viewport hits through `feature_click` (`crates/ui/src/feature_click.rs`) accepting faces, edges, and corners into the draft `start_point` / `exit_point`.\n- Added `start_exit_pick` to `OpUi` (`crates/ui/src/state.rs`) so `Apply`, `Generate`, operation switches, closing properties, tab switches (`SEC_LEADS`), and clearing a point disarm picking cleanly, and `Apply` / `Generate` commit edits through `EditOperationParams` (undoable).\n- Refused fixture entities, non-finite picks, and tilted 2D Contours by name without writing a point.\n- Painted distinct viewport markers in `crates/ui/src/pick_ink.rs` at the contour's resolved `top_z`: a diamond (`Overlay::Pick`) for `start_point` and an X-cross (`Overlay::Region`) for `exit_point`.\n- Recorded the design choices in `docs/decisions/1448-start-exit-viewport-pick.md`.\n\n## Cause\nPR #1938 added typed Start X/Y and Exit X/Y controls on the 2D Contour Lead in / Lead out tab, while viewport picking remained unimplemented (see #1473 item 2 and #1448).\n\n## Tests\nPins:\n- `egui_app::start_exit_rows::tests::the_contour_lead_tab_has_viewport_pick_buttons_for_start_and_exit` (red before fix, green after)\n- `egui_app::start_exit_rows::tests::clearing_a_picked_start_or_exit_resets_it_to_automatic` (red before fix, green after)\n- `egui_app::tests::start_exit_viewport::picking_a_start_point_on_a_wall_regenerates_the_contour_and_undoes` (red before fix, green after)\n- `egui_app::tests::start_exit_viewport::picking_an_exit_point_on_a_wall_applies_and_clear_restores_automatic_exit` (red before fix, green after)\n- `egui_app::tests::start_exit_viewport::clicking_a_fixture_while_picking_start_point_is_refused_by_name` (red before fix, green after)\n- `egui_app::tests::start_exit_viewport::leaving_the_lead_tab_disarms_the_viewport_pick`\n- `start_exit_pick::tests::{marks_draw_for_picked_start_and_exit_and_hide_elsewhere, tilted_contour_pick_is_refused_by_name, non_finite_pick_is_refused_by_name}`\n\nMutation checks (all 6 failed when each guard was reverted/removed and passed when restored):\n- `interact::op_pick_locked` unlock removed -> `picking_a_start_point_on_a_wall_regenerates_the_contour_and_undoes` failed\n- `interact::feature_routed` routing removed -> `picking_a_start_point_on_a_wall_regenerates_the_contour_and_undoes` failed\n- `feature_click::click` handler removed -> `picking_a_start_point_on_a_wall_regenerates_the_contour_and_undoes` failed\n- `op_page` tab-switch disarm removed -> `leaving_the_lead_tab_disarms_the_viewport_pick` failed\n- `start_exit_pick::take` fixture check removed -> `clicking_a_fixture_while_picking_start_point_is_refused_by_name` failed\n- `start_exit_pick::take` tilt check removed -> `tilted_contour_pick_is_refused_by_name` failed\n\nGate after final edit:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (`ui lib` + all 14 affected `camcraft-ui` suites)\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green (0 warnings)\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Unrelated crates outside `gate quick --base upstream/main`, release heavy lanes, and manual live-window interaction. The full shell below was rendered offscreen with the real View3D scene and shipping overlay painter.\n\n## Overlaps\nTouches the same files (different functions/lines; whichever merges second refreshes):\n- `crates/ui/src/feature_click.rs`: PR #2184 (`feature_at`)\n- `crates/ui/src/interact.rs`: PRs #2175 (`ground_grid_lines`), #2146 (`overlay_labels`, `gizmo_segments`, `collect_overlay`)\n- `crates/ui/src/state.rs`: PRs #2187, #2185, #2150, #2149, #2140, #2101, #2077, #1798, #1330\n- `crates/ui/src/lib.rs`: PRs #2192, #2185, #2175, #2149, #1330 (module list only)\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs`: PRs #2185, #2183, #2175, #2149, #2146, #2140, #2101, #2096, #2092, #2090, #2078, #2077, #2068, #1996, #1931, #1330, #1209 (module list only)\n\nChangelog: Add viewport picking and Clear actions for 2D Contour start and exit points\nRefs #1448\n\n\n## Before / after visual evidence\n\nFull-shell offscreen captures of the same seeded 60 × 60 × 30 block, with Start X/Y = 30/0 and Exit X/Y = 60/30 on **Lead in / Lead out**. View3D renders the real scene; the shipping shell paints the controls and overlays. These are review images, not pixel goldens.\n\nBefore: the two affected render files (`start_exit_rows.rs` and `pick_ink.rs`) are from the PR merge-base `e3ca44fa705d71438a8fd8a8efccbafcc2b6517f`. Typed coordinates exist; viewport Pick/Clear controls and point markers are absent.\n\n![Before: typed start/exit controls without viewport picking](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/8ac7ae6de4a2800b3716f9d3aefbc01fbbd7d628/pr-2197/before.png)\n\nAfter: reviewed head `609b4f04d4c221a0dd76be523139207eabdf7366`. The expanded groups show **Pick start**, **Pick exit**, **Clear start**, and **Clear exit**. The start is a diamond at (30, 0); the exit is an X-cross at (60, 30), both on the resolved contour top plane.\n\n![After: viewport pick controls, start diamond and exit X-cross](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/8ac7ae6de4a2800b3716f9d3aefbc01fbbd7d628/pr-2197/after.png)\n\nScrolled to show the exit group (same captures and coordinates):\n\n![Before: start and exit coordinate groups](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/8ac7ae6de4a2800b3716f9d3aefbc01fbbd7d628/pr-2197/before-exit.png)\n\n![After: both expanded point groups and distinct viewport markers](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/8ac7ae6de4a2800b3716f9d3aefbc01fbbd7d628/pr-2197/after-exit.png)\n\nImages are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch. The PR branch contains no screenshots, capture harness, logs, or review evidence.\n",
